* in calculateFlexWeights, it goes: 
1. calculateFlexWeigths
	* actually computes SVD
	* stores number of modes _vSize
	* v_i corresponds to one DoF in the reduced null-space
	* (currently): extracts one torsion-mode vector, the last one
	* maps this mode vector onto all torsions: 

		vector<float> allTorsions = assignWeightsToTorsions(v_i, torsionVector);
		-> this is where we "expand" that mode into the FULL torsion space
		-> creates a full-length torsion vector: std::vector<float> allTorsions(totalTorsionNum, 0.0f);
		-> then fills only the "active" indices: allTorsions[torsionVector[i]] = v_i[i]; 
		-> MEANING: every DOF represented in the SVD that was chosen gets a weight and all other torsions are 0 

